```
Since a membership typically has exactly one role (MEMBER, ADMIN, or OWNER), a user can almost never satisfy both `isTeamAdmin` and `isTeamOwner` simultaneously. This means the variable named `isTeamAdminOrOwner` is effectively always `false`, so team admins and owners who are not themselves the booking organizer or an attendee will be rejected with FORBIDDEN when trying to add guests, defeating the intent of granting admins/owners this permission."}, {"file": "packages/trpc/server/routers/viewer/bookings/addGuests.handler.ts", "line": 525, "severity": "medium", "title": "Team members never notified because evt.team is never populated", "body": "`sendAddGuestsEmails` in email-manager.ts iterates `calendarEvent.team?.members` to notify all team members with `OrganizerAddGuestsEmail`, but the `CalendarEvent` object (`evt`) constructed in `addGuestsHandler` never sets a `team` property. As a result, `calendarEvent.team` is always `undefined` for this flow, so the team-member notification loop is dead code and only the single organizer email (from `booking.userId`) ever receives the organizer notification for team-based bookings, even though other team members may need to be informed guests were added."}, {"file": "packages/trpc/server/routers/viewer/bookings/addGuests.handler.ts", "line": 44, "severity": "medium", "title": "No check that booking is not cancelled before adding guests", "body": "The handler fetches the booking and performs permission checks but never verifies the booking's status (e.g. `CANCELLED`/`REJECTED`). This allows adding guests to cancelled or rejected bookings, which doesn't make logical sense and could trigger calendar/video updates and emails for events that no longer exist."}, {"file": "packages/trpc/server/routers/viewer/bookings/addGuests.handler.ts", "line": 74, "severity": "medium", "title": "Guest emails deduped against existing attendees but not against each other, and comparison is case-sensitive", "body": "`uniqueGuests` is filtered only against `booking.attendees` (`!booking.attendees.some(...)`) and does not remove duplicate entries within the submitted `guests` array itself, nor normalize case. If duplicates (or case-variant duplicates, e.g. `a@b.com` vs `A@B.com`) are submitted in a single call -- which bypasses the client-side `AddGuestsDialog` uniqueness check if called directly via API -- multiple attendee rows with effectively the same email can be created via `createMany`, leading to duplicate attendee records on the booking."}, {"file": "packages/trpc/server/routers/viewer/bookings/addGuests.handler.ts", "line": 167, "severity": "low", "title": "Email send failures are silently swallowed with console.log instead of being logged with context", "body": "```
